# Methodology

## 1. Data Collection

Four datasets were collected containing information about Australian seafood production, commodity values, jurisdictions, and industry sectors.

## 2. Data Cleaning

The datasets were inspected and prepared before being imported into Tableau. Unnecessary fields were removed, unclear column names were renamed, and missing or inconsistent values were checked.

## 3. Data Preparation

The data was filtered to focus on Australia and relevant financial years. Fields were organised into appropriate categorical, numerical, and temporal data types.

## 4. Calculated Fields

Calculated fields were created in Tableau to support:

* Percentage of total value
* Growth rate
* Commodity ranking
* Radial chart coordinates
* Other chart-specific calculations

## 5. Visualisation

Ten charts were created using Tableau. Standard charts were combined with advanced idioms such as treemaps, scatter plots, heatmaps, bump charts, and radial charts.

## 6. Dashboard Design

The charts were arranged into a single dashboard using containers. KPI cards were placed at the top, followed by production and sector comparisons, commodity analysis, and advanced visualisations.

## 7. Interactivity

Filters were added to allow users to explore the dashboard by financial year, commodity, sector, and jurisdiction where applicable.

## 8. Evaluation

The dashboard was reviewed for readability, consistency, visual hierarchy, and whether the charts effectively communicated the main trends in the Australian seafood industry.
